# Intent: The unit half of the question-and-answer games (owner decisions 25 to 27; screens UX17; interface docs/plan/qa-games-firmware.md): riddles, trivia and 20 Questions that the host runs. Tools self.qa.start, self.qa.question, self.qa.verdict, self.qa.end and self.qa.stop; events qa_answer, qa_giveup, qa_again, qa_quit and qa_ended; the state rules in maipai_qa_state_core.h (host-tested with a scripted host); the touch routing with the screens' own rectangles; the shared game-over screen with a saved best per game. The unit never decides what is right: an answer goes out as an event and the host's verdict comes back as a tool call. A riddle's words type at the speaking pace; a touch on them shows them whole; a riddle's answer, sent in the verdict text, stays under the words until Next. No message from the host for two minutes ends the game (host_gone). Full quiet, a lock, an update and another running game refuse or end it. Games never move the head: the file has no motion call.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_qa_game.cc, maipai_qa_game.h, maipai_qa_state_core.h (ours); five small hooks in maipai_games.cc next to the grid games' ones
# Check after a flash: self.qa.start trivia then self.qa.question with four choices: the screen shows the question and four 148 by 56 tiles; a tap on a tile sends the event qa_answer with its number; self.qa.verdict shows the result for 1.2 s with a sound (muted is silent); a gap between tiles does nothing; self.qa.end shows the game-over screen, Play again sends qa_again, Quit sends qa_quit and shows the games page; Stop mid-game sends qa_ended with how quit; two minutes of silence from the host ends it with how host_gone; the riddle's words type at about 14 characters a second and a touch shows them whole. Plain boot memory gate unchanged.
# Kconfig: none (compiled with MAIPAI_GAMES)
# Memory cost: while a question game runs: one 800 byte state in PSRAM, about 15 LVGL objects at an estimated 150 bytes each in internal RAM (the screen is rebuilt, never kept twice), freed when the game ends; flash about 8 KB (estimate). Nothing is held while no game runs.

